{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 314 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "e82af81d88217c3fa627e97df234164bba102388c1088f153af3372e5d832861" :edb/db-before-t 313 :edb/db-after-t 314 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533626 50 #inst "2026-10-04T02:35:57.722Z" 13194139533626 true] [17592186054662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242625 13194139533626 true] [17592186054662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242628 13194139533626 true] [17592186054663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242604 13194139533626 true] [17592186054664 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242611 13194139533626 true] [17592186054664 1020 #edb/ref 17592186242618 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242605 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1089 "q-112815" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1100 "Which root(s) of the polynomial $p(x)=7{x}^{3}+42{x}^{2}$ have multiplicity $2?$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1113 #uuid "c78b7fa0-e6a0-5d03-8538-f39afab9a911" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1138 false 13194139533626 true] [17592186242604 1145 "First, we need to factor the polynomial. \n\nFor this polynomial, we can factor by noting that the greatest common factor of $7{x}^{3}$ and $42{x}^{2}$ is $7{x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =7{x}^{3}+42{x}^{2} \\\\  & =7{x}^{2}(x+6)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the roots and their multiplicities, we look at the factors:\n\n- The factor $x$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=0$ has multiplicity $2.$\n\n- The factor $(x+6)$ has an exponent of $1$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=-6$ has multiplicity $1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only the root $x=0$ has multiplicity $2.$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242606 13194139533626 true] [17592186242605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242607 13194139533626 true] [17592186242605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242608 13194139533626 true] [17592186242605 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242609 13194139533626 true] [17592186242605 1000 #edb/r