\\  & =(3x-1)(3x+1)(3x+1) \\\\  & =(3x-1)(3x+1{)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the roots and their multiplicities, we look at the factors:\n\n- The factor $(3x+1)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=-\\frac{1}{3}$ has multiplicity $2.$\n\n- The factor $(3x-1)$ has an exponent of $1$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ has multiplicity $1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only the root $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ has multiplicity $1.$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242613 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242614 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242615 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242616 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242617 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1041 "selection" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242617 13194139533626 true] [17592186242612 1110 #uuid "69071cb6-d001-5782-aebf-769c85c51a56" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242613 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242613 1111 #uuid "71d201ed-99a4-582c-b72b-bc2f306cac9f" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242614 1034 "x=3" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242614 1111 #uuid "72b7281f-317a-5e2a-800b-1d1b5acf8d6a" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242615 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{3},\\,3" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242615 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242615 1111 #uuid "2d9feeb3-0b9e-5722-95c4-f9d5518c061d" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242616 1034 "x=-3" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242616 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242616 1111 #uuid "cc084344-7f6b-5786-b745-8c5b3fece7dd" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242617 1034 "x=\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242617 1111 #uuid "58f3a0c4-8aea-50ff-93e6-762f0b18d924" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242619 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1089 "q-178256" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1100 "Which root(s) of the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-25x+125$ have multiplicity $2?$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1113 #uuid "d601c130-3a93-5630-8b35-93cbbfae4d1b" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1138 false 13194139533626 true] [17592186242618 1145 "First, we need to factor the polynomial. For this polynomial, we can factor by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & ={x}^{3}-5{x}^{2}-25x+125 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}(x-5)-25(x-5) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-25)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+5)(x-5)(x-5) \\\\  & =(x-5{)}^{2}(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the roots and their multiplicities, we look at the factors:\n\n- The factor $(x-5)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$\n\n- The factor $(x+5)$ has an exponent of $1$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=-5$ has multiplicity $1.$\n\nIn conclusion, only the root $x=5$ has multiplicity $2.$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242620 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242621 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242622 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242623 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242624 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1041 "selection" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242621 13194139533626 true] [17592186242619 1110 #uuid "8371780f-8517-53a5-9208-bef904697560" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242620 1034 "x=-5,\\,5" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242620 1111 #uuid "de338209-971a-5f0e-a02e-cf383c059be3" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242621 1034 "x=5" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242621 1111 #uuid "95af5eee-3d4f-5791-add4-f64c3fe5bc85" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242622 1034 "x=\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242622 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242622 1111 #uuid "d448fb14-b34e-537c-968c-98fd0362973c" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242623 1034 "x=-\\frac{1}{5}" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242623 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242623 1111 #uuid "c9d9c0bb-c2e0-5614-94af-24e5b9f9aea9" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242624 1034 "x=-5" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242624 1111 #uuid "da5421f4-49bc-5fb2-8ee0-8835ea5e40c6" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242626 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1089 "q-271146" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1100 "The multiplicity of the root $x=4$ in the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+14x-8$ is{{field-1}}." 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1113 #uuid "dbb9d4f7-acd8-5a70-85c8-739913bcdc10" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1138 false 13194139533626 true] [17592186242625 1145 "Since $x=4$ is a root of $p(x),$ the factor theorem tells us that $(x-4)$ is a factor of $p(x).$\n\nBecause $(x-4)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-4)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-4)$ using synthetic division:\n\n${x}^{3}$\n${x}^{2}$\n${x}^{1}$\n${x}^{0}$ \n\n \n$4$\n$1$\n$-7$\n$14$\n$-8$\n\n \n\n$↓$\n$4$\n$-12$\n$8$\n\n \n\n$1$\n$-3$\n$2$\n$0$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{p(x)}{x-4}={x}^{2}-3x+2,\n$$\n\nwhich means\n\n$$\np(x)=(x-4)({x}^{2}-3x+2).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =(x-4)(x-1)(x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $(x-4)$ has an exponent of $1$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=4$ has multiplicity $1.$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242626 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242627 13194139533626 true] [17592186242626 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533626 true] [17592186242626 1041 "field-1" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242626 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242627 13194139533626 true] [17592186242626 1110 #uuid "40182997-b4ea-5779-9cc1-9466d7678264" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242627 1034 "1" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242627 1111 #uuid "5aec5e48-3253-5141-8e1e-e752fac1a30a" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1017 #edb/ref 17592186242629 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1089 "q-74233" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1100 "What is the multiplicity of the root $x=1$ in the polynomial $p(x)={x}^{3}+{x}^{2}-5x+3?$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1113 #uuid "c9e57a4e-6690-5ba4-a748-36d2c1e1c0d7" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1138 false 13194139533626 true] [17592186242628 1145 "Since $x=1$ is a root of $p(x),$ the factor theorem tells us that $(x-1)$ is a factor of $p(x).$\n\nBecause $(x-1)$ is a factor of $p(x),$ we know that $(x-1)$ divides $p(x)$ with no remainder. So, to begin factoring $p(x),$ we can divide it by $(x-1)$ using synthetic division:\n\n${x}^{3}$\n${x}^{2}$\n${x}^{1}$\n${x}^{0}$ \n\n \n$1$\n$1$\n$1$\n$-5$\n$3$\n\n \n\n$↓$\n$1$\n$2$\n$-3$\n\n \n\n$1$\n$2$\n$-3$\n$0$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{p(x)}{x-1}={x}^{2}+2x-3,\n$$\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\np(x)=(x-1)({x}^{2}+2x-3).\n$$\n\nWe can factor the quadratic factor even further, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(x) & =(x-1)(x+3)(x-1) \\\\  & =(x+3)(x-1{)}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $(x-1)$ has an exponent of $2$ in the factored form of $p(x).$ So the root $x=1$ has multiplicity $2.$" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242630 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242631 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242632 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242633 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1000 #edb/ref 17592186242634 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1041 "selection" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1104 #edb/ref 17592186242631 13194139533626 true] [17592186242629 1110 #uuid "ffacf150-bd78-5b93-aa64-58b1f56fdc9c" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242630 1034 "3" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242630 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242630 1111 #uuid "6c07e73a-a1ad-54ab-a548-ab79d134f41a" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242631 1034 "2" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242631 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242631 1111 #uuid "140fafc8-f157-5f06-bce3-607c14b160f6" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242632 1034 "1" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242632 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242632 1111 #uuid "e117a576-59f6-5ba3-ad77-6152497b48a1" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242633 1034 "4" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242633 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242633 1111 #uuid "5ad31517-c336-52ea-8eee-6504780eafa6" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242634 1034 "0" 13194139533626 true] [17592186242634 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533626 true] [17592186242634 1111 #uuid "f39195ad-aa7b-5db4-be34-bc6627b9385c" 13194139533626 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-112815" 17592186242604 "q-112815/selection" 17592186242605 "q-112815/selection/2457768122718de57e77bf281f345e9b3101ba474f1bfe0b3b935c89934fe6e6" 17592186242606 "q-112815/selection/6bac05a62229f29eba4498544257eb386a58da0ea736d3d95ca346c883c43950" 17592186242607 "q-112815/selection/7716e3c39a69a249cd41dbb31799405f8c24db067ce959960d178716be565689" 175921862426